2017-11-13 22:40:28		[core]  /buffer  list
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 clear [<number>|<name>|-merged|-all [<number>|<name>...]]
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 move <number>|-|+
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 swap <number1>|<name1> [<number2>|<name2>]
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 cycle <number>|<name> [<number>|<name>...]
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 merge <number>
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 unmerge [<number>|-all]
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 hide [<number>|<name>|-all [<number>|<name>...]]
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 unhide [<number>|<name>|-all [<number>|<name>...]]
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 renumber [<number1> [<number2> [<start>]]]
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 close [<n1>[-<n2>]|<name>]
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 notify <level>
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 localvar
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 set <property> <value>
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 get <property>
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                 <number>|-|+|<name>
2017-11-13 22:40:28		manage buffers
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    list: list buffers (without argument, this list is displayed)
2017-11-13 22:40:28		   clear: clear buffer content (number for a buffer, -merged for merged buffers, -all for all buffers, or nothing for current buffer)
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    move: move buffer in the list (may be relative, for example -1); "-" = move to first buffer number, "+" = move to last buffer number + 1
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    swap: swap two buffers (swap with current buffer if only one number/name given)
2017-11-13 22:40:28		   cycle: jump loop between a list of buffers
2017-11-13 22:40:28		   merge: merge current buffer to another buffer (chat area will be mix of both buffers)
2017-11-13 22:40:28		          (by default ctrl-x switches between merged buffers)
2017-11-13 22:40:28		 unmerge: unmerge buffer from other buffers which have same number
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    hide: hide the buffer
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  unhide: unhide the buffer
2017-11-13 22:40:28		renumber: renumber buffers (works only if option weechat.look.buffer_auto_renumber is off)
2017-11-13 22:40:28		   close: close buffer (number/range or name is optional)
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  notify: set notify level for current buffer: this level determines whether buffer will be added to hotlist or not:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		               none: never
2017-11-13 22:40:28		          highlight: for highlights only
2017-11-13 22:40:28		            message: for messages from users + highlights
2017-11-13 22:40:28		                all: all messages
2017-11-13 22:40:28		              reset: reset to default value (all)
2017-11-13 22:40:28		localvar: display local variables for current buffer
2017-11-13 22:40:28		     set: set a property for current buffer
2017-11-13 22:40:28		     get: display a property of current buffer
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  number: jump to buffer by number, possible prefix:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		          '+': relative jump, add number to current
2017-11-13 22:40:28		          '-': relative jump, sub number to current
2017-11-13 22:40:28		          '*': jump to number, using option "weechat.look.jump_current_to_previous_buffer"
2017-11-13 22:40:28		       -: jump to first buffer number
2017-11-13 22:40:28		       +: jump to last buffer number
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    name: jump to buffer by (partial) name
2017-11-13 22:40:28		Examples:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  clear current buffer:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    /buffer clear
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  move buffer to number 5:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    /buffer move 5
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  swap buffer 1 with 3:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    /buffer swap 1 3
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  swap buffer #weechat with current buffer:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    /buffer swap #weechat
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  jump on #chan1, #chan2, #chan3 and loop:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    /buffer cycle #chan1 #chan2 #chan3
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  merge with core buffer:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    /buffer merge 1
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  unmerge buffer:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    /buffer unmerge
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  close current buffer:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    /buffer close
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  close buffers 5 to 7:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    /buffer close 5-7
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  jump to #weechat:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    /buffer #weechat
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  jump to next buffer:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    /buffer +1
2017-11-13 22:40:28		  jump to last buffer number:
2017-11-13 22:40:28		    /buffer +
2017-11-13 22:41:00		[core]  /window  list
2017-11-13 22:41:00		                 -1|+1|b#|up|down|left|right [-window <number>]
2017-11-13 22:41:00		                 <number>
2017-11-13 22:41:00		                 splith|splitv [-window <number>] [<pct>]
2017-11-13 22:41:00		                 resize [-window <number>] [h|v][+|-]<pct>
2017-11-13 22:41:00		                 balance
2017-11-13 22:41:00		                 merge [-window <number>] [all]
2017-11-13 22:41:00		                 page_up|page_down [-window <number>]
2017-11-13 22:41:00		                 refresh
2017-11-13 22:41:00		                 scroll [-window <number>] [+|-]<value>[s|m|h|d|M|y]
2017-11-13 22:41:00		                 scroll_horiz [-window <number>] [+|-]<value>[%]
2017-11-13 22:41:00		                 scroll_up|scroll_down|scroll_top|scroll_bottom|scroll_beyond_end|scroll_previous_highlight|scroll_next_highlight|scroll_unread [-window <number>]
2017-11-13 22:41:00		                 swap [-window <number>] [up|down|left|right]
2017-11-13 22:41:00		                 zoom [-window <number>]
2017-11-13 22:41:00		                 bare [<delay>]
2017-11-13 22:41:00		manage windows
2017-11-13 22:41:00		         list: list opened windows (without argument, this list is displayed)
2017-11-13 22:41:00		           -1: jump to previous window
2017-11-13 22:41:00		           +1: jump to next window
2017-11-13 22:41:00		           b#: jump to next window displaying buffer number #
2017-11-13 22:41:00		           up: switch to window above current one
2017-11-13 22:41:00		         down: switch to window below current one
2017-11-13 22:41:00		         left: switch to window on the left
2017-11-13 22:41:00		        right: switch to window on the right
2017-11-13 22:41:00		       number: window number (see /window list)
2017-11-13 22:41:00		       splith: split current window horizontally (to undo: /window merge)
2017-11-13 22:41:00		       splitv: split current window vertically (to undo: /window merge)
2017-11-13 22:41:00		       resize: resize window size, new size is <pct> percentage of parent window
2017-11-13 22:41:00		               if "h" or "v" is specified, the resize affects the nearest parent window with a split of this type (horizontal/vertical)
2017-11-13 22:41:00		      balance: balance the sizes of all windows
2017-11-13 22:41:00		        merge: merge window with another (all = keep only one window)
2017-11-13 22:41:00		      page_up: scroll one page up
2017-11-13 22:41:00		    page_down: scroll one page down
2017-11-13 22:41:00		      refresh: refresh screen
2017-11-13 22:41:00		       scroll: scroll a number of lines (+/-N) or with time: s=seconds, m=minutes, h=hours, d=days, M=months, y=years
2017-11-13 22:41:00		 scroll_horiz: scroll horizontally a number of columns (+/-N) or percentage of window size (this scrolling is possible only on buffers with free content)
2017-11-13 22:41:00		    scroll_up: scroll a few lines up
2017-11-13 22:41:00		  scroll_down: scroll a few lines down
2017-11-13 22:41:00		   scroll_top: scroll to top of buffer
2017-11-13 22:41:00		scroll_bottom: scroll to bottom of buffer
2017-11-13 22:41:00		scroll_beyond_end: scroll beyond the end of buffer
2017-11-13 22:41:00		scroll_previous_highlight: scroll to previous highlight
2017-11-13 22:41:00		scroll_next_highlight: scroll to next highlight
2017-11-13 22:41:00		scroll_unread: scroll to unread marker
2017-11-13 22:41:00		         swap: swap buffers of two windows (with optional direction for target window)
2017-11-13 22:41:00		         zoom: zoom on window
2017-11-13 22:41:00		         bare: toggle bare display (with optional delay in seconds for automatic return to standard display mode)
2017-11-13 22:41:00		For splith and splitv, pct is a percentage which represents size of new window, computed with current window as size reference. For example 25 means create a new window with size = current_size / 4
2017-11-13 22:41:00		Examples:
2017-11-13 22:41:00		  jump to window displaying buffer #1:
2017-11-13 22:41:00		    /window b1
2017-11-13 22:41:00		  scroll 2 lines up:
2017-11-13 22:41:00		    /window scroll -2
2017-11-13 22:41:00		  scroll 2 days up:
2017-11-13 22:41:00		    /window scroll -2d
2017-11-13 22:41:00		  scroll to beginning of current day:
2017-11-13 22:41:00		    /window scroll -d
2017-11-13 22:41:00		  zoom on window #2:
2017-11-13 22:41:00		    /window zoom -window 2
2017-11-13 22:41:00		  split window horizontally using 30% of space for the window on top:
2017-11-13 22:41:00		    /window splith 30
2017-11-13 22:41:00		  resize window to 75% of the parent window size:
2017-11-13 22:41:00		    /window resize 75
2017-11-13 22:41:00		  resize vertical split, add 10% in size:
2017-11-13 22:41:00		    /window resize v+10
2017-11-13 22:41:00		  remove the split:
2017-11-13 22:41:00		    /window merge
2017-11-13 22:41:00		  enable bare display for 2 seconds:
2017-11-13 22:41:00		    /window bare 2
